## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-service, tenant-aware, tamper-resistant logging with strict retention and quick rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tamper-evident logging; per-tenant key management; HMAC; Key Vault rotation
- Multi-service sinks; Log Analytics and ADLS Gen2 immutable storage
- Real-time integrity checks; Event Hubs; Canary rollout; incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: sign and write log
function signAndWrite(log, tenantId){
  const key = getKeyFromKV(tenantId);
  const signature = hmacSHA256(log, key);
  writeToSink({log, signature, tenantId});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity without exposing keys?
- How would you handle key compromise and replay attacks?

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to implement zero-trust service-to-service authentication in a multi-tenant Azure environment.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-trust service-to-service authentication using workload identities and OAuth/OIDC tokens
- Kubernetes mTLS via service mesh or sidecar proxies
- Per-tenant Azure Key Vault instances with automated key rotation
- Infrastructure-as-Code policy gates to enforce security baselines (no secrets in configuration, template signing, compliance validation)
- Comprehensive audit trails and User and Entity Behavior Analytics (UEBA) for detecting credential misuse and anomalous access patterns
- Incident response planning with clear rollback procedures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: gateway token validation
function isTokenValid(token, tenantId) {
  const claims = parseToken(token);
  return claims.tenantId === tenantId && 
         claims.iss === 'https://sts.windows.net/' + tenantId &&
         claims.exp > Date.now() / 1000;
}

function validateRequest(req, tenantId) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token || !isTokenValid(token, tenantId)) {
    return { valid: false, reason: 'Invalid or missing token' };
  }
  return { valid: true, claims: parseToken(token) };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical crypto hygiene, CMEK provisioning, tenant isolation, and operations around rotating keys without service downtime.

## Key Concepts

- CMEK per tenant with Azure Key Vault
- Encryption at rest for Cosmos DB with CMEK
- Per-tenant Managed Identities and RBAC
- Key rotation automation and rollback
- Policy and monitoring integration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: create a CMEK and tie to Cosmos DB per tenant
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { KeyClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-keys");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const keyClient = new KeyClient(`https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net`, credential);
await keyClient.createKey("cosmos-cmek-tenantA", "RSA" );
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test key rotation without impacting customers?
- How do you handle key compromise or vault access revocation?
